# AllowanceAgent — progress.md (Sprint 2)

## Sprint 2: Learner Role + HTTP Transport + x402 + Bug Fixes

### Approach Taken
Three parallel workstreams: (A) Learner role with child-scoped data access and source-tagged achievements, (B) dual transport (stdio + HTTP via aixyz) with x402 micropayment gating on manager power tools (learner tools free — B6 override), (C) five bug fixes from Sprint 1 evaluation + Fitbit OAuth + README documentation. OpenMAIC integration is Claude-orchestrated — AllowanceAgent receives achievement data with source provenance, doesn't call OpenMAIC directly. New `release-savings` tool closes the locked-forever gap.

### Workstream A: Learner Role + Source Tagging
- [x] A1: Add Learner role to constants (ROLES, ROLE_HINTS, ROLE_TOOL_ACCESS)
- [x] A2: Add `childName` to Member schema (Learner scoping)
