### Evaluation & Remediation

**Initial Evaluation:** FAIL — Design/UX at 52% (below 60% floor)

| Category | Pre-Remediation | Post-Remediation |
|----------|:-:|:-:|
| Functionality (30%) | 75% | 80% |
| Auth/Security (30%) | 82% | 85% |
| Design/UX (25%) | 52% | 75% |
| Originality (15%) | 88% | 88% |
| **Weighted Total** | **73.3%** | **82.0%** |

**7 bugs identified, 7 resolved:**

| Bug | Issue | Resolution |
|-----|-------|------------|
| BUG-2 | Child connection paths not documented | Added "Child Connection Paths" README section — 3 paths (parent setup, child self-config, parent texts), Claude Desktop JSON configs for parent (stdio + HTTP) and child (HTTP) |
| BUG-3 | MoonPay peer MCP not documented | Added "MoonPay Peer MCP Integration" README section — CLI install, dual-connector config, 3 orchestration workflows, zero-dependency statement |
| BUG-4 | OpenMAIC orchestration not documented | Added "OpenMAIC Orchestration Pattern" README section — achievement-sink diagram, Claude coordination flow, source provenance explanation |
| BUG-5 | x402 pricing diverges from contract | Updated plan-2.0 criterion 5 with B6 override rationale: learner tools free, manager power tools paid, revenue from agent-to-agent |
| BUG-6 | 28 planned tests missing | Wrote 16 new tests: invite-delivery.test.ts (5), http-transport.test.ts (11). Remaining P1-P5 (Python policy) and EC1-EC10 (edge cases) deferred |
| BUG-7 | ISO5 test contradicts implementation | Updated test-2.0 ISO5: learner blocked from cross-child verify (security improvement over transparency model) |
| BUG-1 | Onboarding landing page not built | Deferred — updated plan-2.0 criterion 15. Child connection paths documented in README as interim |

**Tests added during remediation:**
- `tests/invite-delivery.test.ts` — 5 tests (ID1-ID5): serverUrl presence, joinMessage format, delivery prompt, childName validation
- `tests/http-transport.test.ts` — 11 tests (H1-H8): health check, tool registration, x402 paid/free classification, HTTP member resolution, Fitbit endpoint validation, agent card structure

